><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T16:13:22-07:00","id":1072751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1072569#post1072569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could include Important Landmarks, Popular Gathering Spots, Local Legends And Rumors, Influential Figures (Mortal And Supernatural) and Historical Summary.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh man thats a good idea. Updating now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T16:13:56-07:00","id":1072753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1072594#post1072594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MtANWOD/MtA_2ndED_CityWorksheet_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>can be of some help. You could also add some aspirations that would help to pinpoint the mood. Like 'Be welcoming but shallow' , 'Show dominance on streets'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I like this. This will help me alot. I will reedit this sheet with a mix of this information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T19:37:48-07:00","id":1095722,"title":"","content":"Have you had any new ideas for this? Also, you could add the suggestions you liked to the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T07:04:12-07:00","id":1096286,"title":"","content":"Borrowing from DFRPG, a section I really like is &quot;what is the status quo&quot; and &quot;who wants to maintain vs disrupt it&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T12:26:11-07:00","id":1096441,"title":"","content":"To be quite honest, this seems like it'd be less helpful for me, personally, as an ST. I'd want something simple; something that streamlines the city creation process, not creates a million and one more things to fill out.<br /> <br /> The Virtue and Vice concept for city creation is fantastic, because it says so much with so little. It tells you what the default attitude of the person on the street is. Block by Bloody Block and Damnation City also included ideas of framing city regions by giving bonuses to extended rolls based on who and what is there, and that tells you so much about the mood and atmosphere.<br /> <br /> If you want to stat cities quickly, the goal should be to minimize the number of things to stat out and maximize the amount each tells you about the city.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend going with Virtue and Vice. Then, if more is needed, throw in a common mood (a city that's been undergoing a crime wave is very different from one that's in the middle of festival season). After that, list a few major regions and the moods for them, designing them as per Damnation City, until you reach your favoured granularity.<br /> <br /> That's just my feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T12:57:02-07:00","id":1096453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1095722#post1095722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you had any new ideas for this? Also, you could add the suggestions you liked to the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok I did it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:35:58-07:00","id":1123693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1096441#post1096441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be quite honest, this seems like it'd be less helpful for me, personally, as an ST. I'd want something simple; something that streamlines the city creation process, not creates a million and one more things to fill out.<br /> <br /> The Virtue and Vice concept for city creation is fantastic, because it says so much with so little. It tells you what the default attitude of the person on the street is. Block by Bloody Block and Damnation City also included ideas of framing city regions by giving bonuses to extended rolls based on who and what is there, and that tells you so much about the mood and atmosphere.<br /> <br /> If you want to stat cities quickly, the goal should be to minimize the number of things to stat out and maximize the amount each tells you about the city.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend going with Virtue and Vice. Then, if more is needed, throw in a common mood (a city that's been undergoing a crime wave is very different from one that's in the middle of festival season). After that, list a few major regions and the moods for them, designing them as per Damnation City, until you reach your favoured granularity.<br /> <br /> That's just my feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What kind of matrix would you suggest. I'm currently going to try making a custom city tonight so I'm gonna try with my matrix see what I can lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T22:33:17-07:00","id":1123771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1072356#post1072356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random Question What do you think the vice and virtue of Seattle would be ?</div> </div> </div> </div>[$0.02] Innovative/Pretentious for Seattle Washington, whereas I'd say Portland Oregon would be Progressive/Passive-Agressive. <br /> <br /> I am interested in other peoples' point of view/take, as well. [/ $0.02]<br /> <br /> I'll contribute some of the mechanics I've working on in a rough draft in the morning when I have access to my desktop where it is ( on my phone right now).<br /> <br /> They mechanics that interact with the Hunted and Surveilled Conditions from my Homebrew. Adding a mechanic called Turmoil Rating to my Attention/Cover-up mechanics, it measures how violent, dangerous and atrocity filled an area is, a useful thing to track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-02-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T00:46:45-07:00","id":1123793,"title":"","content":"Last (choose your area) scandal and who it effected, gained and lost from it. Scandals are a lot like ripples in a pond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T05:58:56-07:00","id":1123848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1123693#post1123693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of matrix would you suggest. I'm currently going to try making a custom city tonight so I'm gonna try with my matrix see what I can lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, the best way to build a city would be to find something that gives you the ability to say a few <i>definitive</i> statements about a city or town in question. &quot;Everyone has a bachelors or higher&quot;, &quot;People don't stop complaining about the rain&quot;, &quot;The Army base to the north is the source of a lot of ghost stories&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> These statements need to be definitive (i.e. no Barnum statements that invalidate themselves; &quot;Most people are cold and distant, but they all show compassion sometimes&quot;). They're not absolute truths innately, but they're what people think of when they think of the area. That gives you stereotypes for how to present most people - or to emphasize when someone <i>doesn't</i> fit them.<br /> <br /> A Virtue and Vice can be one way to do that, in two fairly easy and succinct statements, but they're not the only way. Once you have the broad details, you can paint in interesting figures as they add something to the setting, and this is the important second detail: The reason a complicated matrix doesn't work is because, not only does it take up too much valuable time, it might not add anything to the story. What does it matter who the mayor is if nothing about them will ever impact the game?<br /> <br /> The point is to create a framework onto which you can hang future details, ideally as you need them, that improve the game and enhance the feeling the environment is meant to evoke. You don't need to know who is in charge of civic planning to know New York is the City of Lights. On the other hand, you might want to think about who is in charge of transportation if you're thinking of, say, New Jersey (cough cough current events cough cough).<br /> <br /> A setting only needs detail insofar as it's interesting. Otherwise, you're spending time talking about Sherlock Holmes's particularly banal choice of wallpaper for twenty pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:42:13-07:00","id":1123925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1123771#post1123771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [$0.02] Innovative/Pretentious for Seattle Washington, whereas I'd say Portland Oregon would be Progressive/Passive-Agressive.<br /> <br /> I am interested in other peoples' point of view/take, as well. [/ $0.02]<br /> <br /> I'll contribute some of the mechanics I've working on in a rough draft in the morning when I have access to my desktop where it is ( on my phone right now).<br /> <br /> They mechanics that interact with the Hunted and Surveilled Conditions from my Homebrew. Adding a mechanic called Turmoil Rating to my Attention/Cover-up mechanics, it measures how violent, dangerous and atrocity filled an area is, a useful thing to track.</div> </div> </div> </div>idk, I'd give them both Passive-Aggressive. There's a reason we call it the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seattle_Freeze\" target=\"_blank\">Seattle Chill/Freeze</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:44:26-07:00","id":1123976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1123925#post1123925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">idk, I'd give them both Passive-Aggressive. There's a reason we call it the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seattle_Freeze\" target=\"_blank\">Seattle Chill/Freeze</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My favorite explanation for the Freeze isn't passive aggressiveness, we just have too many things going on here to be able to handle new people. Everyone I know here has a day job, PLUS some side projects or business AND already has plans for all their free time. New people are just too much of a hassle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:00:10-07:00","id":1124020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1123976#post1123976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My favorite explanation for the Freeze isn't passive aggressiveness, we just have too many things going on here to be able to handle new people. Everyone I know here has a day job, PLUS some side projects or business AND already has plans for all their free time. New people are just too much of a hassle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was due to Infrastructure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:14:04-07:00","id":1124026,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Attention, Cover-Up and Turmoil</b></span><br /> Doing atrocious things get you noticed in a negative way.<br /> <br /> If Attention ever exceeds Cover-Up gain Surveilled Condition<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Attention = Temporary Atrocity + Permanent Atrocity<br /> <br /> Cover-Up is a statistic that represents the effectiveness of concealing one's monstrous nature and activities.<br /> <br /> It is capped by the character's Stability Advantage + local Turmoil rating. A Character's Cover-Up is the amount of Attention they can withstand before they suffer the Surveilled or Hunted Conditions.<br /> <br /> Cover-up = Total of Merits Dots used to conceal monstrous nature + lowest Mental or Social Attribute<br /> <br /> Player needs to describe how these merits contribute to their Cover-Up:<br /> <br /> <b>Potentially Applicable Merits:</b><br /> Allies<br /> Alternate Identity<br /> Anonymity<br /> Fame<br /> Mentor<br /> Mundane Status<br /> Resources<br /> Retainers<br /> Safe Place<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Turmoil</b></span><br /> It is an unfortunate fact some places and times where Atrocities are common enough that pin pointing a specific monster committing Atrocities. This is known as Turmoil. It is rated 0-5 for the place and certain ongoing-circumstances can raise or lower Turmoil while they happen (riots, wars, and crime sprees can increase it, while gentrification, curfews, and increased law enforcement presence can lower it). Major cities with some violent crime reputation range 1 or 2 Turmoil, towns where a single murder would be shocking would be a great example of 0 Turmoil, and areas filled with genocide, thousands of brutal murders annually and warlords constantly battling each other would be examples of 5 Turmoil.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Entities may use Merits of corporeal beings over which it has Manifestations condition for their Cover-up, but are still capped by Stability Advantage + local Turmoil rating.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Example of calculation:</span></b><br /> Vinny, the Mortal Mafia Tough Guy<br /> <b>Permanent Atrocity:</b> 0 (as a non-template Vinny can't acquire Permanent Atrocity)<br /> <br /> <b>Temporary Atrocity: </b>2 (Vinny does a lot of bad things but also regularly dumps his Temporary Atrocity into his Support relationship such as his battered girl friend, his long suffering mother, and other relationships that he has lost over the years. He refrains from dumping Temporary Atrocity into some relationships such as his best friend and co-knee-breaker Joe, or his mafia boss Bruno.)<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity:</b> 4 (Integrity is the number of Support the character retains. Vinny has lost several Support relationships because of his habit of dumping his Temporary Atrocity into them, as well as the Hurt caused by the breaking points he violates. His mother, girlfriend, best friend and mafia boss are his 4 remaining Supports.)<br /> <br /> <b>Turmoil: </b>2 (Vinny works an operates in Chicago IL, and it is not currently going through either abnormally strict law enforcement or riots but is a major city known for violence)<br /> <br /> <b>Intelligence:</b> 1 (Vinny isn't particularly bright, and Intelligence is his lowest Mental or Social stat.)<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Status: Mafia 2 and Alternate Identity 1 (Vinny his standing in the Mafia and his Alias of &quot;Mr. Gray&quot; make sure people don't connect his work to his home life.)<br /> <br /> This adds up to a Cover-Up of 4 with potential maximum of 6, and an Attention of 2. This leaves Vinny vulnerable to gaining the Surveilled Condition by those looking for monstrous activity were he to commit an Atrocity that would be worth 3 or more Temporary Atrocity. Vinny would do well to drop more Atrocity before coming another Atrocity, but he risks losing more Support, thus Integrity. This is the spiral that leads to becoming a Slasher.<br /> <br /> What's the line between monsters, brutal hitmen or serial killers you ask? Very little when you're investigating to find them.<br /> <br /> Most mundane people have a Cover-Up of 2, (Having 'average' as their lowest Mental or Social Attribute, and no merits specifically applied to conceal Atrocity incurring acts) Strangely people with Mental or Social deficiency, thus a Social or Mental Attribute of 1, are more likely to dedicate merits for hypothetical or actual Atrocity incurring acts, thus raising their average Cover-Up. This is likely caused by emotionally or mentally maladjusted individuals being the most likely to resort to Atrocity. Did this just justify some players' tenancy to make min-maxxed combat-monkeys? Yes, with the caveat that it now comes with mechanical disadvantages, additional point costs, and means they cop to playing an &quot;emotionally or mentally maladjusted individual&quot; for a character.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-02-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:27:15-07:00","id":1124033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032976-city-stat-creation-matrix?p=1124020#post1124020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought it was due to Infrastructure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:26:10-07:00","id":1133329,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Name:</b> Iron Ridge</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mood:</b> Drug-Laced Energy</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Theme:</b> Over Indulgence</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Vice:</b> Licentiousness</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Virtue:</b> Ingenuity</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Population:</b> 200,000~</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Top Supernatural Type:</b> Geist</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Merits:</b> Striking Looks 2, Holistic Awareness, Fame 1, Pusher, Spin Doctor, Taste, Sin City*, The Beautiful People *, Surreal* </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Architecture Styles:</b> Spanish And Mediterranean</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Assets:</b> Cultural exports and Tourism</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Districts:</b> Lower Shrum, Lower West Peelrald, Lit Vale, Dellak Market, Little Yupan</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Key Locations:</b> Shelton Beach Front, Ivory Pinnacle Resort, Angelwing Park</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Description: </b>The City is filled with Neon Hues and lights from tike torches. The beachfront and boardwalk ad the most well-kept part of the city to the point you will find many people walking around barefoot in the area with not a care in the world. Past the boardwalk near Angelwing park is where the real face of the city starts to show itself. Drug dealers, addicts, hookers and more. Even here though urban blight is given a pretty mask.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Bio:/History: </b>A city born on the west coast of the United States during the 1800's by Mexico and became a part of the United States during the 1850's. The City itself kept its Spanish/Mediterranean vibe and becoming a party city for the young seeking to let loose. The Main Attraction of the city is Shelton Beach front which Stretches 4 miles. The Beach itself has some of the best waves on the cost. Neon and Tike Torches dot the beachfront while a more postmodern look has taken the city center. All this natural beauty of lively vibes masks a serious drug problem the city has as young people are always found around the city overdosing on various new drugs that are shipped in from Mexico. The city itself has fallen on many hard times but the ingenuity of the people here always pull it out. The current Mayor of the city Sarah C. Ellison seeks to make the city an even more popular by bringing more of the rich and famous to the city by restoring even more of the natural beauty of the land.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Officials</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Mayor:</b> Sarah C. Ellison</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Dept. Mayor: </b>Deanna M. Collier</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Manager: </b>Marilyn W. Lollar</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Assistant City Manager: </b>Darla C. Eden</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>City Attorney: </b>Hannah G. Nichols</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Finance Director: Floyd R. Foreman</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Police Chief: </b>Linda C. Palmer</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Precinct Captains: </b>Racheal R. Houck, Jeffrey J. Cook, Virginia W. Thompson</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Prominent Uniformed Cops:</b> Faustina W. Ware, Rosemary J. Pouliot, Peter L. Thrasher</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>I.A Detectives: </b>Melissa A. Brower, Raymond B. Tharp, Sheryl J. Waddell</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Fire Chief: </b>Lora S. Rodriguez</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Public Works Director: </b>Michael N. Koehler</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Planning Director: </b>George S. Fox</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Economic Development Director:</b> Jennifer T. Langner</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Parks and Recreation Director: </b>Dean M. Swanson</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Newspaper: </b>Zenith Times, The Daybreak Chronicles, The Western Mirror</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>TV Station/Network: </b>WGNO (ABC-26), Wgrz Tv Channel 2, Rhankins, McMullen Ford Inc</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Radio Stations: </b>Laughing Lizards, WKSI-FM RADIO, WTAL Radio 1450 AM</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Gangs: </b>The Fallen Angels, Royal Serpents, Men Of The Night, The Soulless</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Criminal Organizations: </b>The Mortuus Fratrum, The Wildlings</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">*<b>Sin City:</b> The City itself is always encouraging you to sin. Drugs, Drinks, and Sex are all within easy reach and are even offered. People in the city gain back an extra point of willpower when giving into the sin the city encourages the most. It allows lowers the resource dot cost for items that enable the sin.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">*<b>The Beautiful People:</b> The People of the city are quite strange and eclectic that it makes it hard to pick out the strange looking supernaturals in the city. When trying to spot a supernatural take a -1 per level of the merit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">*<b>Surreal:</b> Sometimes a city's vibe is so strong it can change your perception of the world. What was normal is now strange and what's strange is now normal. This merit makes it harder for people to notice the use of supernatural powers or effects at work around them. When rolling for powers being noticed the player gets a bonus to keep their powers hidden per level of this merit.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Timeline:</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">10/26/1870<b> -</b> Town Founded by Oliver Ellison</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">06/04/1872 - Gold/Salt Mine Founded</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">02/04/1873 - The Ivory Spiders Tribe raided the two killing 22 people and setting fire to town hall</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">04/07/1874 - Members of the Ivory Spiders Tribe were hung by the Edward Brooks Father of one of the victims of the raid</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">09/19/1875 - Town Repairs Complete</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">01/08/1877 - Forest Fire Hits the town 44 people die</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">04/27/1877 - Town Rebuilds after fire</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">03/27/1878 - Discovery of an additional Dimond Mine</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">12/14/1888 - New Resources Turn Town in Trading Hub</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">05/07/1889 - Ann E. Johnson and Most of her Children are hung for Witchcraft. Her 3 Youngest Children Escape. Ann Curses Town</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">04/04/1890 - Record Harvest and Large Surplus of Gold Found in Mine</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">05/19/1891 - Oliver Ellison's Oldest Son Gets Married to The second largest family in the state</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">04/29/1895 - Chinese Immigrants make home in the town</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">11/07/1895 - Drug Flood into the town</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">09/06/1901 - Eleanor E. Rodriguez Founds Iron Ridge College</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">11/19/1902 - Iron Ridge College Student Discovers A Plant with potent hallucinogenic properties (Named: Iron sparks)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">02/23/1904 - The Frist Class of Iron Ridge College graduates</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">09/15/1907 - Millionaire Thomas S. Whitlock moves to Iron Ridge and builds the Myrick Mansion</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">02/29/1908 - Thomas S. Whitlock found Murdered on his property</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">10/16/1910 - The Wife of Thomas Whitlock, Rose Whitlock finished her family's house with her 9 children</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">05/13/1914 - Spanish Flu Hits Iron Ridge</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">12/12/1923 - Town put under curfew after Iron Ridge Bank was robbed.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">04/08/1924 - 44 children go missing from the town during a field trip</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">12/22/1926 - The 24 Children are found and returned home known at the Iron Ridge Miracle</span><br /> <sp